- Story & Context: On the winter solstice at the Wat Sai canal junction, twelve elder-crewed sampans lashed themselves together gunwale-to-gunwale, routing their synthesizers through a shared floating antenna composed of discarded cathedral stained-glass fragments. As the sub-bass frequencies rolled across five miles of winding backwaters, hundreds of silver canal carp leaped into the air in rhythmic sync, prompting nearby vegetable vendors to drop their oars and cast fragrant jasmine garlands onto the women’s mixing desks. The choir of grandmothers watched the sun finally break the tree line in ribbons of violet and peach, singing in unison through tape-fluttered reverbs: "Let the light strike the crack where the kickdrum hides."
